    "result_text": "Both findings addressed, tests green.\n\n## Changes\n\nI agreed with both findings \u2014 they're structural tidy-ups, not behaviour changes:\n\n1. **Duplicated `\"61\"` magic string** \u2014 the `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` key now uses the existing `DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE` constant (`NATIONAL_LENGTHS.put(DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE, 9)`), so the Australian country code has a single source of truth. A maintainer changing the default now touches one spot.\n\n2. **Validation inlined into the normalize flow** \u2014 extracted the per-country length loop into a private `assertNationalLength(digits, raw)` helper with its own Javadoc. `toE164` now reads as a clear sequence: strip \u2192 resolve country code \u2192 range check \u2192 national-length check \u2192 return.\n\n**Test result** \u2014 acceptance behaviour intact, suite green:\n\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```",
