    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is small and reasonably placed, but two structural points would make it more coherent with the existing code:\n\n1. **Duplicated `\"61\"` magic string.** `DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE = \"61\"` already exists, and now `\"61\"` reappears as a `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` key representing the same concept (the Australian country code). A maintainer changing the default country would have to remember to touch both spots. Reference the existing constant (e.g. `NATIONAL_LENGTHS.put(DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE, 9)`) so the single source of truth is preserved.\n\n2. **Validation concern inlined into `normalize`.** `normalize` now handles default-code substitution, the `\\d{8,15}` range check, *and* the per-country length loop. The new block is a self-contained validation step with its own comment; extracting it into a small private helper (e.g. `assertNationalLength(digits, raw)`) keeps `normalize` reading as a sequence of clear steps and matches the \"one responsibility per unit\" grain of the rest of the class.\n\nNeither is a correctness issue (per the task, I'm not judging that) \u2014 both are purely about keeping the unit boundaries and DRY-ness natural for a maintainer of this file.",
